WEBVTT

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:08.480
Q: What comes to mind when you think of bookstore staff?

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.730
<i>This is out of the blue, but here's a question:</i>

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.710
<i>What comes to mind when you 
think of bookstore staff?</i>

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.190
They seem kind.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:13.830
<b>Mom</b>

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:13.830
<b>Sister</b>

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:31.140
What are your thoughts on bookstore staff?

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.110
Gentle. Pleasant. Sweet.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:21.960
<b>Acquaintance</b>

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.610
If it's a chick, she's gotta have 
black hair, glasses, and a huge rack.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.040
If it's a dude, he's gotta 
have glasses and be lanky.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.830
<i>Those are </i>desires<i>.</i>

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.000
<b>Dad</b>

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.800
Please don't get angry...

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.860
Bored

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:29.380
It seems easy, not very 
stimulating, and monotonous.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.140
<b>Dad</b>

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.140
<i>Wait, wait! That's too harsh.</i>

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.130
<i>Although, that might have been 
what I'd have thought, too...</i>

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.980
<b>Staff Only</b>

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.550
<i>until I started working at a bookstore.</i>

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.630
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:54.870
<b>Staff Only</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.870
The Handsome Guy is First in Line

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.920
Oh, Honda, good, you're here.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.240
We're sold out of <i>King**m</i>, and we're 
getting a shipment in the afternoon.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.280
Help me stock up later.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.340
Sure, got it.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.260
How many copies per customer 
maximum for <i>V J*mp</i>?

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.990
Someone bought out all of our 
stock the other day, so two max.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.970
A live action movie adaptation?!

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.610
Mr. Sales

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:09.470
Yes.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.270
Again?!

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.930
Again.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:13.500
Why do people ask for <i>V J*mp</i> so much?

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:16.740
<i>Now that I'm working at a bookstore,</i>

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.260
Apparently people like the bonus material.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.700
Wait, who's in the cast?!

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.820
<i>I think it's a frantic, busy,
 very stimulating job.</i>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.310
Huh, looks like we didn't get too many copies.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.540
There it is.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.420
I think this is the right book.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.600
Yes, yes, that's the one.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.700
Thank you.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.000
My son's become such an anime nerd lately.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.010
He seems to be enjoying it, 
so I got interested, too.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.020
But there are so many, I had 
no idea where to even look.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.980
I never knew there were so many manga.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.000
<i>This is my workplace.</i>

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.370
<i>We call it a bookstore, but it 
specializes mostly in comics.</i>

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.120
<i>And these days, most of
 the excitement I experience</i>

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.440
<i>from customers who are 
just way too eccentric.</i>

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.300
Help at the cashier, please.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.380
Coming!

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.910
Thank you.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.470
Can I help the next customer?

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:06.210
Hi.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.210
<i>Hot dude!</i>

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.540
<i>What a handsome old man!</i>

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.230
<i>Do you see it?</i>

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.920
<i>An aura that makes you go, 
"Huh? Is he a Hollywood actor?"</i>

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.590
<i>A halo of light...</i>

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:19.130
<i>A weighty background music...</i>

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.170
<b>*Hallucination</b>

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.170
<b>Auditory 
hallucination</b>

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.220
<i>A godliness that can alter your five senses!</i>

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.180
<i>I know this pose.</i>

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.290
<i>A lot of people show me their phone 
screens when they can't find a book.</i>

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.670
Excuse me, I'm just looking for this manga.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.470
The "I can kind of understand English,
 but I can't speak it" face

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.010
<i>English!</i>

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:41.280
I can't seem to find it anywhere.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.630
<b>Audio</b>

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.630
<b>Japanese</b>

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.450
My daughter asked me to buy it.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:47.500
She told me not to come home until I find it.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:52.020
<i>You can see a hint of nauseous 
exhaustion through his smile.</i>

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:56.880
<b>Nauseous exhaustion...</b>

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.320
<i>I'm intrigued by this book that's 
apparently so hard to find, though.</i>

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:04.430
The ways and nuances in which a book may not be at a bookstore

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:04.430
- No reprint planned (basically comatose)

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:01.130
<i>Books with no planned reprint, no stock
 at the publisher, out of print...</i>

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:04.430
- No stock at the publisher (basically near-death)

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:04.430
- Out of print (basically dead)

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:04.430
- E-book (Doppelganger from a parallel universe)
* Sudden reanimation is possible in all cases. *

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:03.650
<i>There's tons of books that can no longer be found.</i>

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.550
<i>If that's the kind of book he's looking 
for, I can at least tell him that.</i>

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.650
Ah, pardon me, I was looking for a picture.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:15.610
Sure.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.980
<i>I totally wasn't expecting </i>this<i>!</i>

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:31.180
Dojinshi (Self-published books)

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:30.290
<i>Dojinshi, or self-published books, 
are not available at our store.</i>

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.090
<i>But that aside...</i>

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.140
<i>This is totally </i>Gint***<i>!</i>

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.060
<i>It's an adult book, through and through!</i>

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.360
<i>Yeesh, tentacles!</i>

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.850
<i>Wait a second, let's figure 
out what I want to say.</i>

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:43.320
<i>Hey, mister, you're in 
kind of a pickle, here.</i>

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.890
<i>This is a dojinshi, and one 
